= Sizhu Lu
[sizhu_lu@berkeley.edu]

~~~
{}{img_left}{images/profile.png}{}{160}{160}{}
Welcome to my homepage!

I am postdoctoral researcher at Stanford University, where I am very fortunate to work with Professors [https://lihualei71.github.io/ Lihua Lei], [https://gsb-faculty.stanford.edu/guido-w-imbens/ Guido Imbens], and [https://jiafengkevinchen.github.io/ Kevin Chen]. 

Before joining Stanford, I received my Ph.D. in Statistics from the Department of Statistics at UC Berkeley, where I was very fortunate to be advised by Professor [https://sites.google.com/site/pengdingpku/ Peng Ding]. I was also very fortunate to be advised by Professor [https://sites.google.com/view/tingye Ting Ye] on some projects. Previously, I received my B.S. in Mathematics and Applied Mathematics and B.A. in Finance from Peking University. I also spent time working in the world of finance and real estate after college and received my Ph.D. in Business Administration from Haas School of Business, UC Berkeley, where I was very fortunate to be advised by Professor [https://faculty.haas.berkeley.edu/amir/ Amir Kermani]. Here are links to my [https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=jmdmQu0AAAAJ&hl=en&oi=ao Google Scholar profile] and [https://github.com/sizhu-lu GitHub].

I will join the [https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/statistics-datascience/index.html Department of Statistics \& Data Science] at Carnegie Mellon University as a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Fall 2027.

~~~

